\subsection{Time-budget Pareto}

The cartesian linear-HPO baselines make the cost of external preprocessing
optimization explicit.  PLS-HPO used 600 preprocessing combinations with five
trials each and produced 36 complete three-seed datasets; the observed total
time across successful rows is 162.4 h, with median per-run total time
984.90 s.  Ridge-HPO used ten trials per combination and produced 35 complete
datasets; the observed total is 184.1 h, with median per-run total time
2024.55 s.  By contrast, ASLS-AOM-compact-cv5 has a median fit time of 1.89 s
in the multi-seed run, FastAOM-sparse-mkr-compact 2.48 s, and
FastAOM-single-chain-compact 1.86 s.  AOMRidge-Blender is heavier
(median 960.08 s) but remains competitive with Ridge-HPO while retaining a
single auditable operator-kernel model.

