are favourable on the 14-dataset overlap, with median balanced-accuracy gains
from 0.163 to 0.175 and 13--14 wins.  The global compact classifier is the
single AOM-Ridge classification row used in the main text because it has the
largest median gain.

\section{Failure Modes}

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Failure-mode ledger summary.  Rows with no finite RMSEP correspond
to data-quality estimator failures in the HPO campaign; finite rows summarize
absolute-error spread across logged variants.}
\label{tab:sup_failure_modes}
\small
\input{tables/table_failure_modes.tex}
\end{table}

The failure ledger separates three categories.  The first category is
denominator pathology, represented by QUARTZ in the manifest: absolute errors
remain meaningful, but ratios are not used because the reference denominator
is essentially zero.  The second category is estimator input failure, seen in
the two FUSARIUM rows listed above; these rows contain NaN values for the
linear HPO estimators.  The third category is ordinary model mismatch, where
all models return finite predictions but the RMSEP spread is large.  Examples
include Brix, Rice Amylose and LMA rows, where branch correction, derivative
choice or default-bank operators can dominate the compact-bank selection.

\section{Seed Stability}

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Seed-stability diagnostics for the multi-seed AOM-PLS and top5
AOM-Ridge runs.  Winner-change datasets count datasets whose best member of
the listed family changes across seeds.}
\label{tab:sup_seed_stability}
\small
\input{tables/table_seed_stability.tex}
\end{table}

AOM-PLS dataset-level RMSEP rankings are highly correlated across seeds:
mean seed-pair Spearman correlations are 0.996--1.000 for the main variants.
The nonzero median seed CV for compact AOM variants reflects internal
selection changes, and 18 datasets change the winning member of the
AOM-PLS/PLS family across seeds.  The top5 AOM-Ridge rows are deterministic
on the recorded split/random-state representation, so their
seed-pair correlations are 1.000 and the family winner does not change.
FastAOM is deterministic for a fixed train/test split and configuration; its
seed0 evidence should therefore be read as chain-space evidence rather than
split-resampling evidence.

