-the current overlap with Ridge-HPO is unfavourable (ratio 1.173, 6/25 wins);
-it is therefore treated as an efficiency-oriented exploration rather than the
-headline Ridge selector.
-
-The Ridge result supports the operator-geometry view: adapting the spectral
-Gram matrix is at least as important as adapting the cross-covariance in PLS,
-and the Blender selector gives a robust middle ground between single-operator
-selection and broad superblock mixtures.
