+total of 0.2 h.  On median total time, this is a factor of about 508.  In
+candidate evaluations, the contrast is 3000 trial fits per PLS-HPO
+dataset/seed versus 45 compact-bank CV evaluations for AOM-PLS.
+
+Ridge is different because the selected Blender selector is heavier.  It
+still improves over Ridge-HPO on the completed overlap, and its median total
+time is 960.71 s compared with 2024.55 s for Ridge-HPO.  The result is not
+that every AOM selector is instant; it is that strict-linear preprocessing
+can be represented as a model geometry rather than as a blind external
+pipeline loop.
 
