-The strict distinction is essential.  SNV divides by sample-specific
-statistics; MSC and EMSC estimate correction parameters relative to a
-reference; ASLS estimates a baseline through an iterative asymmetric
-criterion.  These are valid preprocessing branches, but they are not fixed
-matrices that can be inserted into the operator algebra outside a fold.
+The outside-scope examples are important.  SNV uses sample-specific centering
+and scaling.  MSC and EMSC estimate correction parameters relative to a
+reference.  ASLS estimates a baseline through an iterative asymmetric
+criterion.  These transformations are allowed in the benchmark, but only as
+branches fitted inside each calibration fold.  The selected PLS result uses
+such a branch followed by the compact strict-linear AOM bank.
 
