+The cartesian-HPO baselines are intentionally strong and expensive.  They
+enumerate 600 preprocessing combinations.  PLS-HPO uses five trials per
+combination; Ridge-HPO uses ten trials per combination.  These baselines were
+evaluated on the subset of datasets that completed within the compute budget;
+the LUCAS\_SOC rows did not complete, and two FUSARIUM rows failed estimator
+checks because the response contained NaN values.
 
