+All selection steps are internal to the calibration set.  External test sets
+are preserved when available; otherwise deterministic SPXY or stratified
+splits are used \citep{kennard1969computer,galvao2005method}.  RMSEP is the
+primary regression metric.  Because response scales differ across traits,
+aggregate regression results use paired RMSEP ratios.  Classification uses
+balanced accuracy.  Paired tests use one-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank tests
+with Holm correction within the displayed family.
+
+The cartesian-HPO baselines are intentionally strong and expensive.  They
+enumerate 600 preprocessing combinations.  PLS-HPO uses five trials per
+combination; Ridge-HPO uses ten trials per combination.  These baselines were
+evaluated on the subset of datasets that completed within the compute budget;
+the LUCAS\_SOC rows did not complete, and two FUSARIUM rows failed estimator
+checks because the response contained NaN values.
 
