+\subsection{Covariance identity for one-shot AOM-PLS}
+
+For centered $\X$ and $\Y$, the transformed PLS cross-covariance for operator
+$\A_b$ is
 \begin{equation}
-  (\X\A_b\transpose)\transpose\Y = \A_b\X\transpose\Y .
+  (\X\A_b^\transpose)^\transpose\Y
+  =
+  \A_b\X^\transpose\Y .
   \label{eq:cov_identity}
 \end{equation}
-This identity supports covariance-space SIMPLS and adjoint NIPALS
-implementations without materializing every transformed spectrum matrix.
+Equation~\ref{eq:cov_identity} is the core simplification.  It means that a
+bank of strict linear preprocessings can be screened by acting on
+$\X^\transpose\Y$, without fitting one full PLS model for every transformed
+matrix.
 
