-$\T=\X\Z$ and the final coefficient matrix
+where $\mathbf W$ are weights, $\mathbf P$ are spectral loadings,
+$\mathbf Q$ are response loadings and $+$ denotes the Moore--Penrose inverse.
+In AOM-PLS, a component may be selected in a transformed space.  If the
+transformed-space direction is $r_a$ under operator $\A_b$, its
+original-wavelength direction is
 \begin{equation}
-  \B = \Z(\mathbf P\transpose \Z)^+ \mathbf Q\transpose .
