+(\texttt{AOMRidge-Blender-headline-spxy3}).  It combines several strong
+operator geometries through internal validation rather than committing to one
+noisy winner.  GCV, local-neighbourhood and global compact selectors are
+mathematically described in the supplement; only Blender is kept in the main
+results because it has the best refreshed win-rate and median ratio on the
+largest paired denominators.
 
