+Ridge: median RMSEP ratio 0.913 on $N=52$ datasets with 44/52 wins and
+Holm-adjusted $p=2.8\times10^{-6}$.  It also improves over the completed
+Ridge-HPO subset, with median ratio 0.956 on $N=34$, 27/34 wins and
+$p=0.011$.
+
+The Ridge result supports the operator-kernel view.  In Ridge, preprocessing
+changes the regularized sample geometry.  Blender is the best main selector
+because it combines strong operator geometries through internal validation
+while preserving a single deployable Ridge model.
 
